{
  "query": "You support the platform team at mcnz.com and must design a pattern to keep two Cloud Firestore databases in different Google Cloud projects synchronized. Updates must replicate in both directions so that a write in either database is delivered to the other within 15 seconds. Which approach should you implement?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Schedule recurring gcloud firestore export and import operations with Cloud Scheduler every 30 minutes",
      "explanation": "This runs timed jobs that export one database and import it into the other on a fixed schedule.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Publish document change events from each Firestore to Pub/Sub and trigger Cloud Functions to apply the mutations to the peer project",
      "explanation": "This uses event driven processing where Pub/Sub messages invoke Cloud Functions that write the corresponding updates into the other database.",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Build a Cloud Data Fusion pipeline that reads from and writes to both Firestore instances for two way sync",
      "explanation": "This designs a Data Fusion integration flow to pull from each Firestore source and push updates to the other.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Set up Datastream to capture changes from Firestore in each project and replicate them to the other Firestore",
      "explanation": "This uses Datastream change data capture to move updates between sources and targets.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
